'''Lil Portals''' are entities that only appear in {{s|Mausoleum}} and {{s|Gehenna}}. They continuously spawn fly and spider enemies until they are destroyed. There can be a max of 4 spawned monsters alive at once. Monsters they can spawn include:
{{entity table | Attack Fly, Moter, Sucker, Ink, Level 2 Fly, Full Fly, Spider, Swarm Spider, Big Spider, Level 2 Spider, Small Crazy Long Legs, }}

== Lil Portal (Flies Only) ==
There is a variant of the Lil Portal with the ID 306.1.1 that looks and behaves identically to regular Lil Portals but will only spawn Fly related monsters from its regular pool.

{{clear}}{{dlc clear}}

== Entrance Portal ==
A special version of the Portal (dubbed the "Entrance Portal" to avoid confusion) serves as the entrance to {{s|The Void}}. It is found in {{s|???}}, but can also be found after defeating {{E|Mom}}, {{E|Mom's Heart}} / {{E|It Lives!}}, {{E|Isaac}} / {{E|Satan}}, {{E|???}} / {{E|The Lamb}}, {{E|Mega Satan}}, or {{e|Mother|r+}}.
The Entrance Portal room in ??? gets darker the closer the player is to the portal.

== Unlockable [[Achievement]]s ==
{{achievement text | Black Hole }}

== Notes ==
* [[Status Effects#Charm|Charming]] a Portal with {{i|Mom's Eyeshadow}} or similar items will cause the Portal to spawn permanently charmed enemies similar to the {{i|Friendly Ball}}.
** As a result, a permanently charmed {{E|Death's Head}} can spawn from charmed Portals on Chapter 3 and remain permanently invulnerable. This is the only known method of charming an invulnerable enemy.
* If a portal is spawned in {{s|???}}, {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Dark Room}} or {{s|Home}} via {{dlc|a+}} [[Debug Console]], the Portal will despawn a few seconds before spawning any monster.
* If Portals aren't unlocked, certain enemies will spawn in their rooms instead, depending on the floor the room is in. For instance, Frowning Gapers spawn as Portal placeholders on Chapter 1 floors, whereas Vises spawn as Portal placeholders on Chapter 4 floors.
* It is often wise to instantly run into portals with orbitals after entering the room, if possible. Catching the small window timeframe for this almost always results in their instant death without any consequences.

